================================================================================
HOST-SIDE STATE (already landed in Project-M — no action needed in this repo)
================================================================================

Transport / contract (host receiver: html/projectm-external-pcm.js):
  - Accepts `{ type: 'pcm', buffer: Float32Array, channels?: 1|2, sampleRate? }`
    over BOTH window.postMessage (primary) and BroadcastChannel("projectm-audio")
    (legacy fallback). `channels` defaults to 2; for stereo, `buffer` must be
    interleaved L/R with even length.
  - postMessage origin allow-list: https://mod.1ink.us, https://flac.1ink.us,
    https://test.1ink.us (+ localStorage `externalPcmOrigins` override).
  => The sender should send `channels: 1` explicitly (AnalyserNode time-domain is
     mono) and may include `sampleRate: ctx.sampleRate`, exactly as the diff above.

Audio-only / projectM-embed mode (`?projectm=1`):
  - The host now appends `?projectm=1` when opening the player as a pure decoder,
    for BOTH the popup launcher (withProjectMAudioFlag() in
    html/projectm-audio-player.js; popup window.name target = `flac-player`) and
    the iframe embeds in projectm_panel.1ink / projectm_panel2.1ink.
  - The in-repo loader shell html/flac-player/index.html detects the flag BEFORE
    loading the bundle and exposes:
        window.__projectMAudioOnly === true
        window.__projectMEmbed === true
        document.documentElement[data-projectm-audio-only="1"]
  => The bundle should read either the `?projectm=1` query param or these globals
     and, when set: SKIP WebGPU pipeline init (projectM draws the visuals) and show
     a compact transport-only UI. When the flag is absent, keep the full standalone
     WebGPU UI (no regression). Tear down the RAF bridge + BroadcastChannel on
     pause/stop/close (cancelAnimationFrame(r); t.close();).
